schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: Digital Garden (seedling / budding / evergreen)
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A living, linked collection of notes tended over time rather than
    published once, using openly-marked growth stages so readers can tell a
    rough sketch from a settled, maintained answer.
  source_traditions:
    - >-
      Mike Caulfield's 2015 talk "The Garden and the Stream," which
      contrasted the chronological "stream" of feeds/chat with the
      slowly-cultivated "garden" of linked, revisited knowledge
    - >-
      Maggie Appleton's digital-garden writing, which popularized the
      seedling (🌱) / budding (🌿) / evergreen (🌳) growth-stage convention
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Used in this article as the organizing metaphor for community knowledge
    commons, paired with a concrete stack recommendation (Obsidian + Quartz +
    GitHub) and a named "gardener" role responsible for tending.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - wiki (typically filled once, less emphasis on revisiting/pruning)
    - document dump / shared drive ("a compost heap nobody turns")
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      Garden ≠ document dump — the difference is three habits (linking over
      filing, openly-marked growth stages, active tending), not which tool
      is used
    - >-
      Stream ≠ garden — chat/feeds are chronological and ephemeral; a garden
      is linked and revisited
  tensions:
    - >-
      "growth stage" maturity marking (seedling/budding/evergreen) is a
      different vocabulary from this toolkit's own K1 maturity axis
      (raw/draft/candidate/reviewed/...) — both solve the same problem
      (letting readers trust the right things) but do not map 1:1
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating the seedling/budding/evergreen convention as just a labeling
    scheme misses its actual function: it is a permission structure that
    lets contributors publish before perfect, which is the harder cultural
    change than the labels themselves.
  maturity: raw
  public_use: source-linked-unreviewed
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/knowledge-gardens.md
    transformation: synthesized
    authorship: ai-assisted
